summary:
  A file qmllint gave up on passes the lint again, because nothing asks
  whether the name planted at its end was reported.

history:
  qmllint exits 0 and prints nothing about a file it stopped reading, which
  is also what it does for a file with nothing wrong in it. The lint took
  the one for the other twice: four files and 16 766 lines by 2026-09-20,
  and main.qml, FullRepresentation.qml and SyncEngine.qml again by 2026.43,
  where a wrong member name planted in each was reported 0 times. The pass
  now ends a copy of every file with one more object that reads a name
  nothing declares, and a file where that read is not reported fails.

target:
  scripts/qmllint_gate.py

find:
      if probe_line is not None and not seen:

replace:
      if probe_line is not None and not seen and False:

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_a_file_qmllint_gives_up_on_fails_by_name,
  which lints a file whose only fault is a const inside a callback, and by
  tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_the_verdict_on_one_file on a report made
  by hand, where there is no Qt.
